#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70dec8f-9828-5fe7-bdb7-47e6557fc889" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c2115b7-3deb-582b-a761-e79b45a72ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3,$ $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416443} {:answer/id #uuid "72a19815-f7b7-56e9-badf-ea7b9e73091b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6,$ $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416453} {:answer/id #uuid "872eaed5-b7dd-5088-8dd0-359491c4f657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3,$ $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416457} {:answer/id #uuid "93dcd708-1476-51b0-ac1f-9db7ca101165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9,$ $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416459} {:answer/id #uuid "949e815d-00ae-5171-94b0-1798b1a30df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9,$ $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c2115b7-3deb-582b-a761-e79b45a72ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3,$ $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416443} :answer-field/id #uuid "533bf985-e003-5103-b11c-9c7a7c723cb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab4ca253-4533-55ea-9cf5-518c8864d1f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-139508" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}9-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (9-\\lambda )(9-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{9}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70dec8f-9828-5fe7-bdb7-47e6557fc889" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f0d752a-b826-5c64-be10-12da661ba4f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368915} {:answer/id #uuid "013ec41c-cc86-5fe4-b29a-accf164dceb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$13$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368916} {:answer/id #uuid "24eac0e8-069f-5b0b-9420-f802df54dfb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{13}$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368917} {:answer/id #uuid "a9aa8865-fb8b-5614-b9f2-9c3837814ef1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368918} {:answer/id #uuid "7be86b9d-e96c-5fac-9a1f-8fb3684e2c62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24eac0e8-069f-5b0b-9420-f802df54dfb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{13}$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368917} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd34787a-f30f-575c-9f6f-407c026f6c03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40523132-fd0a-5a78-90b5-ce48c89eb124" :question/math-academy-id "q-95317" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}9-\\lambda  & -6 \\\\ -6 & 4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (9-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda -4\\lambda +36-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -13) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =13,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{13} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2bf7196-b681-5ff6-bf16-24acefa04e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17453e7d-2501-500c-988d-632cc6dfbc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368922} {:answer/id #uuid "3e7fa423-ce11-5e4b-941d-b20daa102519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368923} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf839ad-4dca-5536-a5e6-2102abbf3175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368924} {:answer/id #uuid "d0871187-035d-52b5-b781-f70eaa3bf24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368925} {:answer/id #uuid "0183a8ef-a247-5fec-a72f-23430bb57861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0871187-035d-52b5-b781-f70eaa3bf24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368925} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd50738-594a-50f0-9455-2e79aec8430d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "80bd1a5b-eef3-57d3-b7a8-ea1d67708737" :question/math-academy-id "q-95364" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}10-\\lambda  & -6 \\\\ -6 & 10-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(10-\\lambda )-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda +100-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda +64 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -16) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =16,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{16}=4 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2bf7196-b681-5ff6-bf16-24acefa04e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57ba2282-d4ab-5fbf-9130-d06a2eed65a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385854} {:answer/id #uuid "b45ecc1a-07a7-50a1-a446-cf4a96064ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385855} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a83de7-3a30-52e2-a29e-09bdd3418bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,\\,2,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385856} {:answer/id #uuid "01e6f9da-3643-528a-9879-9df01fb0203d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385857} {:answer/id #uuid "d58280f6-ca95-52bf-80d9-6a8986b3c8bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57ba2282-d4ab-5fbf-9130-d06a2eed65a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385854} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a01643e-564d-5068-bf87-5773a11495bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "63c30a7c-7d2d-5a6c-adcf-5b929543dd1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95369" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 8-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 8-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )((5-\\lambda )(8-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2bf7196-b681-5ff6-bf16-24acefa04e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fab31e-219e-5d18-813a-a8d06acc3248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415548} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5778c2-893f-5035-ae58-7208c5dc0a69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415556} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8616be-5d4c-5647-8715-109f64e7adf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415558} {:answer/id #uuid "c1276a11-417f-5453-89d9-104681d36b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415563} {:answer/id #uuid "cf324114-3726-57f4-b073-13b1533f0488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf324114-3726-57f4-b073-13b1533f0488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415565} :answer-field/id #uuid "2503f0e3-6a58-532b-b8da-6c772b852974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2512d16d-c375-5bf3-9c3b-0ab4d79702bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-95374" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -4) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =4,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
